## Elsa v3 BuildProcessWorkflow Implementation Plan

### Context

Problem: Manufacturing workflow orchestration incomplete. Two activities (GetBuildActivity, PublishBuildStatusActivity) are stubbed  /backend/src/FactoryApp.Workflows/Activities/, but Elsa DI not registered, no workflow definitions exist, and GraphQL mutations don't trigger workflows.

Scope: Implement complete BuildProcessWorkflow: Build → Parts → TestRun → Release with 5 activities, error handling, compensation logic, persistence, and state recovery.

Constraints:
- Primitive-only state in workflow vars (Guid, string only) — fetch fresh data on activity execution
- Elsa v3.5.3 API limitation: ActivityExecutionContext lacks SetVariable/GetVariable — use input/output properties as workaround
- Return DTOs from GraphQL, never raw EF Core entities
Max GraphQL depth: 5 layers
- Integration tests must use real SQL Server, not mocks

---

### Phase-Based Implementation Plan

Phase 1: Elsa Infrastructure Setup (Program.cs)

File: /backend/src/FactoryApp.WebApi/Program.cs (line 99-103)

Current state: Elsa registration commented out due to v3.5.3 API limitations (documented).

Changes:
Uncomment and populate Elsa registration section (lines 99-103)
2. Add builder.Services.AddElsa(elsa => elsa.AddActivitiesFrom<Program>().AddWorkflowsFrom<Program>())
3. Register activities in DI:
  - builder.Services.AddScoped<GetBuildActivity>()
  - builder.Services.AddScoped<PublishBuildStatusActivity>()
  - builder.Services.AddScoped<ProcessPartsActivity>() (new)
  - builder.Services.AddScoped<TriggerTestRunActivity>() (new)
  - builder.Services.AddScoped<AwaitTestCompletionActivity>() (new)
4. Configure Elsa persistence: .UseSqlServer(connectionString) for workflow state storage
5. Add IWorkflowHost injection for workflow management

Note: Shelved patch at /backend/.idea/.idea.FactoryApp/.idea/shelf/feat__register_Elsa_v3_workflows_and_implement_GetBuildActivity↓and_PublishBuildStatusActi/shelved.patch lines 201-209 shows intended registration pattern.

---

Phase 2: Implement Missing Activities

Location: /backend/src/FactoryApp.Workflows/Activities/

Files to create (3 new + improve 2 existing):

2.1 Update GetBuildActivity.cs

- Replace TODO comments (lines 45, 55) with proper output handling
- Set output property: Build = build (when Elsa API available, use context.SetVariable)
- Add proper error logging via ILogger DI
- Return early on Guid parse failure with error completion

2.2 Update PublishBuildStatusActivity.cs

- Improve error handling (lines 76-79): log exceptions instead of silent fail
- Add ILogger DI for auditability
- Validate enum parsing doesn't throw (wrap in try-catch)

2.3 Create ProcessPartsActivity.cs (NEW)

```csharp
[Activity(Category = "Manufacturing", Description = "Validate parts exist")]
public class ProcessPartsActivity : Activity {
    private readonly FactoryDbContext _dbContext;
    public string? BuildId { get; set; }
    public bool PartsValid { get; set; } // Output

    protected override async ValueTask ExecuteAsync(ActivityExecutionContext context) {
        // 1. Fetch fresh Build + Parts (primitive-key-only pattern)
        var build = await _dbContext.Builds
            .Include(b => b.Parts)
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(b => b.Id == Guid.Parse(BuildId!));

        // 2. Validate parts exist
        PartsValid = build?.Parts?.Count > 0;

        // 3. Complete
        await context.CompleteActivityAsync();
    }
}
```

2.4 Create TriggerTestRunActivity.cs (NEW)

```csharp
[Activity(Category = "Manufacturing", Description = "Publish test run event")]
public class TriggerTestRunActivity : Activity {
    private readonly ITopicEventSender _eventSender;
    public string? BuildId { get; set; }
    public string? TestRunId { get; set; } // Output (generated UUID)

    protected override async ValueTask ExecuteAsync(ActivityExecutionContext context) {
        var testRunId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();
        TestRunId = testRunId;

        // Publish event to subscribers
        await _eventSender.SendAsync("testRunTriggered",
            new TestRunTriggeredEvent { BuildId = Guid.Parse(BuildId!), TestRunId = testRunId });

        await context.CompleteActivityAsync();
    }
}
```

2.5 Create AwaitTestCompletionActivity.cs (NEW)

```csharp
[Activity(Category = "Manufacturing", Description = "Wait for test completion event")]
public class AwaitTestCompletionActivity : Activity {
    public string? TestRunId { get; set; }

    protected override async ValueTask ExecuteAsync(ActivityExecutionContext context) {
        // Async wait for testRunCompleted event signal
        // Implementation: subscribe to ITopicEventReceiver or use Elsa event-wait pattern
        // For now: placeholder — will receive signal from SubmitTestRun mutation
        await context.CompleteActivityAsync();
    }
}
```

Key Pattern for All Activities:
- Inject dependencies in constructor (DbContext, ITopicEventSender, ILogger)
- Use public string properties for inputs (Guid as string)
- Store output in properties (Elsa v3.5.3 workaround — upgrade to context.SetVariable in v3.6+)
- Fetch fresh domain data on each execution (primitive-only pattern from workflow-integration.md)
- Log all state transitions for auditability
- Graceful error handling with logging

---
Phase 3: Create BuildProcessWorkflow Definition

File: /backend/src/FactoryApp.Workflows/WorkflowDefinitions/BuildProcessWorkflow.cs (NEW)

```csharp
public class BuildProcessWorkflow : WorkflowBase {
    protected override void Build(IWorkflowBuilder builder) {
        builder
            .Root = new Sequence {
                Activities = new List<Activity> {
                    new GetBuildActivity { BuildId = new Input<string>(args => args.BuildId) },
                    new ProcessPartsActivity { BuildId = new Input<string>(args => args.BuildId) },
                    new TriggerTestRunActivity { BuildId = new Input<string>(args => args.BuildId) },
                    new AwaitTestCompletionActivity { TestRunId = new Input<string>(...) },
                    new PublishBuildStatusActivity {
                        BuildId = new Input<string>(args => args.BuildId),
                        NewStatus = new Input<string>("Released")
                    }
                }
            };
    }
}
```

Workflow Trigger: BuildCreated mutation (mapped to BuildMutation.CreateBuild)

Compensation Logic (Rollback on Failure):
- Add compensation activities after each main activity
- Compensation chain: PublishBuildStatus(Failed) ← Rollback ← TriggerTest(Cancelled) ← RollbackParts ← etc.
- Store compensation state in workflow variables
- Log all compensation steps

---
Phase 4: Wire GraphQL Integration

File: /backend/src/FactoryApp.GraphQL/BuildMutation.cs (line 115)

Changes in CreateBuild mutation:
1. Inject IWorkflowHost in method signature
2. After await dbContext.SaveChangesAsync() (line 113), add:

```csharp
// Start BuildProcessWorkflow with new build ID
var workflow = await workflowHost.ExecuteAsync(
    workflowName: "BuildProcessWorkflow",
    input: new Dictionary<string, object> { { "BuildId", build.Id.ToString() } }
);

loggingService.LogWorkflowStart("BuildProcessWorkflow", build.Id, workflow.Id);
```
3. Return build payload immediately (workflow runs async)
4. Add error handling: if workflow start fails, log but don't break mutation

---
Phase 5: Persistence & State Recovery

File: /backend/src/FactoryApp.WebApi/Program.cs (Elsa config section)

Changes:
1. Configure Elsa persistence backend: .UseSqlServer(connectionString)
2. Enable workflow history: .WithWorkflowHistoryEnabled()
3. Add startup logic to resume incomplete workflows:
var host = app.Services.GetRequiredService<IWorkflowHost>();
await host.ResumeAsync(filterPredicate: w => w.Status == WorkflowStatus.Running);

New Service: Create WorkflowRecoveryService in /backend/src/FactoryApp.Services/
- Method: ResumeIncompleteWorkflows() — called on app startup
- Query incomplete workflows from persistence store
- Resume each workflow with its saved state
- Log recovery metrics

---
