6.2 Workflow Integration Tests

File: Workflows/BuildProcessWorkflowTests.cs (NEW)

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task ExecuteWorkflow_BuildCreated_CompletesAllActivities() {
    var buildId = Guid.NewGuid();
    var build = new Build { Id = buildId, Status = BuildStatus.Pending };
    context.Builds.Add(build);
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();

    var result = await workflowHost.ExecuteAsync(
        "BuildProcessWorkflow",
        new { BuildId = buildId.ToString() }
    );

    Assert.Equal(WorkflowStatus.Finished, result.Status);

    // Verify DB state changed
    var updated = await context.Builds.FindAsync(buildId);
    Assert.Equal(BuildStatus.Released, updated.Status);
}
```

6.3 Failure Scenario Tests

File: Workflows/BuildProcessWorkflowCompensationTests.cs (NEW)

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task ExecuteWorkflow_ProcessPartsActivityFails_TriggersCompensation() {
    // Setup: Build with no parts (ProcessParts should fail)
    var buildId = Guid.NewGuid();
    var build = new Build { Id = buildId, Parts = new List<Part>() };
    context.Builds.Add(build);
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();

    var result = await workflowHost.ExecuteAsync("BuildProcessWorkflow", new { BuildId = buildId.ToString() });

    Assert.Equal(WorkflowStatus.Failed, result.Status);

    // Verify compensation: Build status should be set to "Failed"
    var failed = await context.Builds.FindAsync(buildId);
    Assert.Equal(BuildStatus.Failed, failed.Status);
}
```

Test Setup:
- Use real SQL Server (docker-compose) via integration test connection string
- Auto-create test databases per test run
- Seed fixtures with deterministic GUIDs
- Clean up after each test (database disposal)

---
### Critical Implementation Details

State Management

- DO: Store only Guid/string in workflow variables → fetch fresh data on activity execution
- DON'T: Store complex objects (Build entity) in workflow state — will become stale
- Pattern: Guid.Parse(activity.BuildId) → dbContext.Builds.FindAsync(buildId) in each activity

Error Handling & Compensation

- Catch exceptions in activity ExecuteAsync → log details
- On failure, trigger compensation workflow (reverse activities in reverse order)
- Store compensation state as primitive keys
- Example: If ProcessParts fails, skip to PublishBuildStatus(Failed)

Real-Time Updates

- Leverage existing Hot Chocolate subscriptions + ITopicEventSender
- Activities publish events (buildStatusChanged, testRunTriggered, etc.)
- Frontend Angular subscriptions receive updates via WebSocket

Versioning

- Workflow definition versioned by Elsa (version field in DB)
- In-flight workflows complete with their version
- New builds start with latest workflow version
- Allows schema changes without breaking old workflows

