### Verification Checklist

1. Elsa DI Registered:
  - dotnet build succeeds
  - IWorkflowHost resolvable in DI container
  - Activities register without errors
2. BuildProcessWorkflow Executable:
  - Run: dotnet test backend/FactoryApp.Tests/Workflows/BuildProcessWorkflowTests.cs
  - Workflow starts and completes all 5 activities
  - Build status transitions: Pending → Processing → Parts Validated → Testing → Released
3. GraphQL Integration Works:
  - pnpm dev starts backend + frontend
  - Execute createBuild mutation
  - Check backend logs: "WorkflowStart: BuildProcessWorkflow, buildId=..."
  - Run dotnet test backend/FactoryApp.Tests/BuildMutationTests.cs — should pass
4. Compensation Logic:
  - dotnet test backend/FactoryApp.Tests/Workflows/BuildProcessWorkflowCompensationTests.cs
  - Inject failure at ProcessPartsActivity
  - Verify compensation chain executes, Build status → Failed
5. State Recovery:
  - Start workflow, pause it mid-execution (mock long delay)
  - Kill app, restart
  - Verify workflow resumes and completes

---

### Known Constraints & Workarounds

| Constraint | Workaround | Future Fix |
|---| ---| ---|
| Elsa v3.5.3 lacks SetVariable/GetVariable API | Use public properties for input/output | Upgrade to Elsa v3.6+ |
| Activity state isolation | Fetch fresh data per activity execution | Document in workflow-integration.md |
| Async event waiting (AwaitTestCompletion) | Use event publish/subscribe pattern | Elsa v3.6+ async bookmark support |
| No built-in compensation | Manual compensation workflow definition | Elsa v3.6+ compensation support |
